  "notes": "{怠|なま}ける means to be lazy or slack off, with negative connotations.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Usually intransitive: {怠|なま}けている (being lazy)\n- With object: ⟦{仕事|しごと}→仕事：00480_shigoto⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{怠|なま}ける (to slack off from work)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {怠|なま}けて⟦ばかり→〜ばかり：02006_bakari⟧⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧: to always be slacking off\n- ⟦{勉強|べんきょう}→勉強：00770_benkyou⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{怠|なま}ける: to neglect one's studies\n- {怠|なま}けず⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{働|はたら}く→働く：00503_hataraku⟧: to work without slacking\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {怠|なま}け⟦{者|もの}→者：12734_mono⟧: lazy person, slacker\n- ⟦{怠惰|たいだ}→怠惰：08191_taida⟧: laziness, indolence (noun/na-adj)\n- ⟦{怠|おこた}る→怠る：03936_okotaru⟧: to neglect (more formal)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦さぼる→サボる：09295_saboru⟧: to skip, play hooky (more colloquial, often for specific occasions)\n- ⟦ぐうたらする→ぐうたら：noentry⟧: to loaf around (casual)",
